{
  "_doc": [
    "Colours for blender/paint_statues.py, taken from reference/polychromy.md (sections 2 and 3). Edit here only: the pipeline reads colours from nowhere else.",
    "pigments: named sRGB colours (hex). A region's color is a pigment name or a hex value.",
    "alpha = paint coverage over bare marble (0 bare, 1 opaque). Skin is a thin glaze (ganosis), 0.2-0.5.",
    "Lookup for a region of a statue: statues.<key>.<region name> -> statues.<key>.<region kind> -> default.<region name> -> default.<region kind>.",
    "Region kinds: skin, hair, beard, garment, attribute, support, sandals, plinth; face decals: eyebrows, eye_white, eye_corner, iris, iris_ring, pupil, lid_line, lips.",
    "recess / crest (optional): colour mixed into the paint in folds and drill channels / on crests and ridges, mix = strength 0..1.",
    "garment.border: band inside the garment along its edges, width_rel = band width / statue height; lines = ornamental lines in the band (pos, width as fractions of the band width, 0 = garment edge).",
    "wear: 0..1, paint thinner on ridges than in recesses; wash_noise: low-frequency alpha variation.",
    "plinth.mode: bare (alpha 0) or band (painted band just below the top of the scan's plinth; band_rel = band height / statue height)."
  ],
